8. IMPLEMENTATION CHALLENGES AND SOLUTIONS
-------------------------------------------

8.1 MAJOR CHALLENGES

8.1.1 Thread Safety with Mutexes
Challenge: DownloadTask containing mutex made object non-copyable
Solution: Used shared_ptr<DownloadTask> for safe cross-thread sharing

8.1.2 Tracker Synchronization
Challenge: Maintaining consistent state across two trackers
Solution: WAL-based replication with best-effort propagation

8.1.3 Chunk Integrity
Challenge: Ensuring downloaded chunks are not corrupted
Solution: SHA1 hash verification with automatic retry from different peers

8.2 DESIGN DECISIONS

8.2.1 Protocol Design
Decision: Simple text-based protocols over binary
Rationale: Easier debugging and development at the cost of slight overhead

8.2.2 Chunk Size
Decision: Fixed 512KB chunks
Rationale: Balance between network efficiency and memory usage

8.2.3 Concurrency Model
Decision: Thread-per-chunk download model
Rationale: Simple implementation with good parallelism for moderate loads

9. DEPLOYMENT AND OPERATIONAL CHARACTERISTICS
----------------------------------------------

9.1 SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS

9.1.1 Hardware Requirements
- Minimum: 2GB RAM, 10GB storage
- Recommended: 4GB RAM, 50GB storage
- Network: 100Mbps+ for optimal performance

9.1.2 Software Dependencies
- C++11 compatible compiler (g++ 4.8+)
- OpenSSL development libraries
- POSIX-compliant operating system

9.2 OPERATIONAL CHARACTERISTICS

9.2.1 Startup Sequence
1. Start trackers (order doesn't matter)
2. Trackers replay WAL and establish sync connection
3. Clients connect to any available tracker
4. System ready for operations

9.2.2 Shutdown Sequence
1. Clients automatically logout and cleanup
2. Trackers persist final state to WAL
3. System can resume from last consistent state



